Q1. No dependency management - If the first script fails, the second script may still run and process incomplete data.
No automatic retries- If a database or API temporarily fails, the script stops completely unless someone reruns it manually.
No monitoring or visibility-There is no dashboard to check which step failed or why it failed.
Q2. Airflow adds scheduling, dependency management, retries, monitoring, logging, and workflow orchestration to Python pipelines
Q3. In a logistics company:
First task → validate shipment file
Second task → transform records
Third task → load into warehouse
If validation fails because the file is missing, transform and load should NOT run. Otherwise bad or incomplete data enters the warehouse. 

